# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GTS pipeline — what must NOT go into the repository.
#
# Two rules behind everything below:
#   1. campaign DATA never leaves the machine it was analysed on. Track exports
#      carry team codes and GPS traces; settlement lists carry population
#      estimates. None of it belongs in a public GitHub repo.
#   2. anything the pipeline GENERATES is rebuilt on every run, so committing
#      it only creates merge conflicts and bloat.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.Python

# ---- secrets --------------------------------------------------------------
# Streamlit secrets are configured in the Cloud dashboard, never committed.
.streamlit/secrets.toml
.env
*.pem
*.key

# ---- campaign data (NEVER commit) -----------------------------------------
# Raw GTS track exports and the merged file built from them.
Tracks_*.csv
merged_tracks.csv
*_tracks.csv
tracks.parquet

# Planned settlement lists / DIPs.
settlement*.csv
*settlement*.csv
!*/settlement_template.csv

# ---- pipeline outputs (regenerated every run) -----------------------------
Day*_out*/
*_outputs/
outputs/
.ckpt/
charts/
maps/
*_settlement_visitation.csv
team_deploy_day_*.csv
time_spent_day_*.csv
flagged_teams_day_*.csv
*_ERM_Analysis.xlsx
*_Report.pptx
*_Report.docx
*_Post_Implementation_Report.docx
gridded_ta_day_*.parquet
gridded_ta_day_*.gpkg
visited_day_*.geojson
not_visited_day_*.geojson

# ---- QGIS working layers --------------------------------------------------
# Exported analysis layers, not pipeline inputs. ~100 MB and rebuilt in QGIS.
# The three BOUNDARY files the app needs are whitelisted below.
*.sqlite
!LGA.sqlite
!Ward.sqlite
!state.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.gpkg-journal
*.qmd

# ---- reference material, not needed to run --------------------------------
# Kept locally for comparison; excluded to keep the repo installable.
#
# "Post Implementation Report sample.pdf" is excluded too, despite stage 7
# auto-detecting it. It is a real Nasarawa PIR containing photographs of eHA
# staff at evening review meetings, and this repository is public. Stage 7
# never opens the file — it checks the path exists and writes the filename
# into the .docx metadata comment; the report is built entirely by
# python-docx. Without it, stage 7 logs "No Post Implementation Report sample
# found — using the built-in default layout" and produces identical content.
# Keep your local copy: `--pir-template` still accepts it when running
# locally.
*sample*.pdf
*sample*.xlsx
GTS_Pipeline_Workflow_eHA.pptx
*_title_preview.pptx
pipeline_flow_diagram.png

# ---- test scratch files ---------------------------------------------------
# test_daily_time_spent.py writes this when run from the repo folder.
dt.csv
tr.csv
tr2.csv

# ---- editor / OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
~$*
